{% extends "project/base.html.twig" %}

{% block title %}About{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="about">
        <h3>ORM Database Q&A</h3>
        <h4>What database does this adventure game have?</h4>
        The game uses an SQLite database. 
        <h4>Tell us a bit about whats in the db?</h4>
        This game has 4 tables in the db.<br>
        <b>Rooms</b><br>
        Stores all the rooms in the game - including their id, name and their room description.
        <br>
        <b>Path</b><br>
        Stores all possible path from any room, that paths direction and which room it connects to as well as if that path requires an item.
        <br>
        <b>Choices</b><br>
        Stores every single choice in the game - which room they're available in, if that choice yields an item, 
        if the player needs an item to see this choice and, of course, the dialogue the player gets when interacting with this choice.
        <br>
        <b>Item</b>
        Stores a list of items available in the game - just their id, name and their description.
        <h4>How about that Entity Relationship - how are the tables connected?</h4>
        Well, in short: A Room have paths and choices connected to it. Choices sometimes require an item to be interacted. Choices sometimes rewards an item.
        <br>
        A Room have an <i>id</i> that connects to a Paths <i>'from_room'</i> and to a Choices <i>'room'</i>.
        <br>
        A Room can har zero or many Paths (0..N) while each Path leads from one Room to another.
        <br>
        A Room have one or more Choices (1..N), every Choice belongs to exactly one Room.
        Some Choices requires an item before they become available to interact with.
        <br>
        Some Choices rewards an Item, each Items are connected to exactly one Choice.
    </div>
    <div class="about"><h3>ER Diagram</h3><br>
        <img src="{{ asset('img/project/mvcERdiagram.png') }}" alt="ER Diagram">
        <h4>Did you test the database?</h4>
        I did! I managed to make a mock object of Doctrine, the entity and repository. 
        Then I made a 'stub' to test the methods. It wasn't easy to wrap my head around, but I tried to make meaningful tests.
    </div>
{% endblock %}